    "done_when": "a new module reckon/crew/follow_checkpoint.py reads and atomically writes a per-project, per-session checkpoint in the follower directory holding the stream path, the stream's identity (enough to tell a replaced or truncated file from the same one), the offset after the last delivered line and the state last reported per run; _follow_watch_lines in reckon/cli.py writes it as it delivers and, when no environment checkpoint was handed across a reload, reads it at start: on a continuable checkpoint it seeks to the offset, delivers every line written since with the stream's own timestamps and emits no baseline, so a re-arm with nothing new prints nothing; on a replaced or truncated stream it emits only runs whose state differs from the checkpoint's reported state, each stamped with the run's recorded transition time, never the attach time; with no checkpoint it emits the baseline stamped per run, and a run whose stream has advanced past its start renders working, never dispatched (if that state is computed outside the fence, name the function and line in follow_ons); tests/test_follow_rearm_continues.py, with a synthetic config home and producer stream, arms a follower, delivers transitions, ends it at its lifetime, appends transitions while nothing is attached, re-arms with no environment checkpoint, and asserts exactly the gap transitions arrive in order with their stream timestamps and no row for an unchanged run; a second test asserts a re-arm with no intervening transition emits no line; a third replaces the stream between arms and asserts only changed runs are emitted with recorded times and no running run renders dispatched; the tests assert the real follower directory under the user's config home is unchanged; two declared mutations are applied and each observed to fail with its log recorded: the re-arm ignores the durable checkpoint, and replayed rows are stamped with the attach time; the existing follow tests pass unchanged; ruff on reckon/cli.py reports no more findings than at base",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "a follower re-arm continues from its durable checkpoint instead of replaying a baseline",
